          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Experts will deliver lectures and recommend methods of quitting tobacco, which is known to be responsible for 100,000 deaths per year in Pakistan. Globally, some five million people die every year as a result of smoking. Lung and mouth cancer are the two leading causes of cancer deaths in Pakistan and both are considered to be strongly associated with tobacco use.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
